  "tagline": "Swedish artist (1862–1944)",
  "bio": "Hilma af Klint was a Swedish artist and mystic whose paintings are considered to be among the first major abstract works in Western art history. A considerable body of her work predates the first purely abstract compositions by Kandinsky, Malevich, and Mondrian. She belonged to a group called \"The Five\", a circle of women inspired by Theosophy who shared a belief in the importance of trying to contact the \"High Masters\", often through séances. Her paintings, which sometimes resemble diagrams, were a visual representation of complex spiritual ideas.",
